---
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How the Kalaris Labs website handles personal information, consent-gated PostHog analytics, error monitoring, and your choices about data collection."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy' },
  ]}
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-shell">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal / 02</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Effective 29 September 2026</p>
        <p class="page-lede">
          This policy explains what information this website handles, why we use
          it, and the choices available to you.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-copy">
        <section>
          <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            Kalaris Labs operates kalarislabs.com and is responsible for the
            personal information described in this policy. You can reach us
            about anything in it at
            <a href="mailto:hello@kalarislabs.com">hello@kalarislabs.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Information you send us</h2>
          <p>
            If you email us, apply to work with us, or submit a contact form, we
            receive the information you provide. This may include your name,
            email address, organisation, message, résumé, portfolio, and any
            other material you choose to send.
          </p>
          <p>
            On the Fellowship page, the name you enter to generate your badge is
            stored only in your browser. It reaches us only if you continue to
            the application, where it is used to prefill the application form or
            email.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Analytics and error replays</h2>
          <p>
            Both of the following run only after you choose “Allow” in the
            analytics preferences. Until then, neither is loaded.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>PostHog product analytics</strong> may collect page views, clicks
              and other interactions, device and browser details, approximate location,
              and session information, and may record session replays. Form inputs
              and content marked private are masked in recordings.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Sentry error replays</strong> keep a short, masked record of
              recent activity on the page. It is sent only if an error occurs, so
              we can see what led to the problem. Text is masked and images and media
              are blocked.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You can change your choice at any time through “Analytics
            preferences” in the footer. Withdrawing consent stops collection
            from that point on.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Your analytics choice</strong> is saved in your browser’s local
              storage so we do not ask on every page. This is necessary for the preference
              to work.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>PostHog</strong> sets cookies and local storage entries (names
              beginning with <code>ph_</code>) to recognise a returning browser,
              only after you allow analytics.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Your Fellowship badge name</strong>, if you enter one, is
              kept in local storage so your badge persists. You can remove it by
              clearing this site’s data in your browser.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Cloudflare</strong> may set strictly necessary cookies to protect
              the site from abuse and automated traffic.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Security and technical data</h2>
          <p>
            Our hosting and security providers may process IP addresses, request
            metadata, device information, and security signals to deliver the
            site, prevent abuse, and diagnose failures. The site runs on
            Cloudflare infrastructure and may use Cloudflare Turnstile on forms.
            Sentry receives technical error and performance reports. These
            include recorded page activity only when you have allowed it, as
            described in section 3.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. How we use information, and why</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              to respond to questions, applications, and press enquiries,
              because you asked us to or to take steps before working with you;
            </li>
            <li>
              to operate, secure, and fix the website, based on our legitimate
              interest in running a safe and reliable service;
            </li>
            <li>
              to understand how the site is used, only with your consent, which
              you can withdraw at any time; and
            </li>
            <li>to comply with law and protect our rights.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Service providers</h2>
          <p>
            We share information only as needed with providers that help us run
            the site and communicate, including Cloudflare, PostHog, Sentry, and
            Resend. They process information under their own terms and privacy
            commitments. We do not sell personal information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We keep information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the
            purpose for which it was collected, including communication,
            security, record-keeping, and legal obligations. Retention periods
            vary by the type of information and service involved.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Your rights and choices</h2>
          <p>
            You may decline or withdraw optional analytics at any time. You may
            also ask us to access, correct, update, or delete personal
            information we hold about you and, where the law provides for it,
            nominate someone to exercise these rights on your behalf. We may
            need to verify your identity before completing a request.
          </p>
          <p>
            To make a request or raise a grievance, email
            <a href="mailto:hello@kalarislabs.com">hello@kalarislabs.com</a>
            with “Privacy” in the subject line. We will respond within the time required
            by applicable law. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may
            complain to a data protection authority, such as the Data Protection Board
            of India or, in the EU or UK, your local supervisory authority.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. International processing</h2>
          <p>
            Our service providers may process information in countries other
            than your own. Where required, we use the safeguards made available
            by those providers and applicable law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Children</h2>
          <p>
            This website is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly
            collect personal information from anyone under 18 without the
            consent of a parent or guardian.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. Changes and contact</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy as the site and our services change. The
            date above identifies the current version. For privacy questions or
            requests, email
            <a href="mailto:hello@kalarislabs.com">hello@kalarislabs.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
